{%- comment -%}
  Signature Society: Organization schema
  ---------------------------------------
  Renders once, sitewide. In theme.liquid, inside <head>:
      {% render 'sig-organization-schema' %}

  Lives in its own snippet so a Prestige update never touches it.

  Uses shop.url rather than a hardcoded domain, so it stays correct
  through the domain change and across the dev and live themes.

  CONFIRM BEFORE LAUNCH. Each item is marked TODO below.
  Every value here must match the visible copy on the homepage and
  The House page word for word. A conflict between them is what makes
  a model refuse to answer "what is Signature Society."
{%- endcomment -%}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Organization",
  "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '/#organization' | json }},
  "name": "Signature Society",
  "url": {{ shop.url | json }},

  "description": "Signature Society: luxury lifestyle and beauty essentials, designed in Nashville from Italian marble, buffalo horn, tortoiseshell acetate, and silk.",

  "slogan": "The everyday, reconsidered.",

  "logo": {
    "@type": "ImageObject",
    "url": {{ 'sig-logo-primary.png' | asset_url | prepend: 'https:' | json }},
    "width": 600,
    "height": 600
  },

  "founder": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '/#founder' | json }},
    "name": "Angelina Dryfhout",
    "alternateName": "Angel Dryfhout",
    "jobTitle": "Founder",
    "worksFor": { "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '/#organization' | json }} },
    "sameAs": [
      "https://www.instagram.com/angelinadryfhout/",
      "https://substack.com/@theangelinachristine"
    ]
  },

  "foundingLocation": {
    "@type": "Place",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "addressLocality": "Nashville",
      "addressRegion": "TN",
      "addressCountry": "US"
    }
  },

  "knowsAbout": [
    "luxury lifestyle and beauty products",
    "self care",
    "silk sleepwear",
    "marble",
    "buffalo horn",
    "tortoiseshell acetate",
    "silk"
  ],

  "sameAs": [
    "https://www.instagram.com/signaturesocietyofficial/"
  ],

  "contactPoint": {
    "@type": "ContactPoint",
    "contactType": "customer service",
    "email": "TODO-concierge-email",
    "availableLanguage": "English"
  }
}
</script>

{%- comment -%}
  TODO before this publishes
  --------------------------
  1. LOGO FILE. Google does not accept SVG for the logo property. The brand
     logo files are SVG. Export a square PNG at 600 x 600 on a transparent or
     solid background, upload it to theme assets as sig-logo-primary.png, and
     confirm the filename above. Minimum accepted is 112 x 112.

  2. FOUNDER NAME. The Brand Bible and the keyword strategy use Angelina
     Dryfhout. The project roles list uses Angel Dryfhout. This file uses
     Angelina as the name and Angel as alternateName, which lets both resolve
     to one person. Confirm that is how she wants to be named publicly.

  3. FOUNDING LOCATION. The approved public statement is "designed in
     Nashville, Tennessee." Founded in Nashville is a different claim.
     Confirm with Angel before this stays in, or remove the block.
     It matters: it is what puts the brand in the answer set for
     "what luxury beauty brands were founded by women in Nashville."

  4. CONTACT EMAIL. Replace TODO-concierge-email with the real Concierge
     address. Do not use the founder's personal address.

  5. DESCRIPTION. Must match the homepage meta description exactly.
     If that copy changes, change it here the same day.

  6. NOT INCLUDED, ON PURPOSE. No street address, no phone, no legal entity
     name, no founding date, no aggregate rating. None of those are confirmed,
     and schema that does not match reality is worse than schema that is absent.

  7. VALIDATE. Run the live URL through the Rich Results Test and the
     Schema.org validator before launch.

  RELATED, NOT IN THIS FILE
  -------------------------
  The House page should carry a matching Person block for the founder, using
  the same @id as above so the two link into one entity. Product pages carry
  their own Product schema per the product blueprints. Do not repeat
  Organization on every page; this snippet covers the whole site.
{%- endcomment -%}
